  ('gender_category_debate','Gender history and women\'s history: the dichotomies exchange','Whether gender history extends or displaces women\'s history. Pierson\'s 1991 essay opens on the turn to deconstruction and Scott; Sangster (1995) drew replies from Iacovetta and Kealey and from Dubinsky and Marks, and a rejoinder (1996). The Left History texts were not read here; positions are not characterised beyond their titles.',['ruth_roach_pierson','joy_parr','joan_sangster','franca_iacovetta','linda_kealey','karen_dubinsky','bryan_d_palmer'],['palmer_1990','pierson_1991','parr_1995','sangster_1995','iacovetta_kealey_1996','dubinsky_marks_1996','sangster_1996']),
